## Findings
1. blocking — brief:89 The prototype’s `readSucceeded` is module-global, not mount-scoped: after an earlier successful screen, a serve restart leaves a stale stored token; navigating to a new screen gets `401`, but saving the replacement token leaves `rereadOwed` false and the real screen failed. Replace brief:89 with: `| 6. A read’s refusal in the current routed-screen mount | each route/readEpoch mount begins with no successful screen read; local refusal, its pre-success 401 and a refused stream owe one re-read, while a later refusal after that mount loaded does not | beginReadMount (specified), called by App from useLayoutEffect on route/readEpoch before screen reads, resets the mount marker; getJSON, subscribeLive and rereadAfterTokenSaved refuse and consume it as stated; W-501-b3 pins a prior successful screen followed by a stale-token failure on a newly mounted screen |`. [severity: S1] [design: changes] [class: spec×promise-unattainable-under-accepted-domain] — check: apps/web/test/w501.test.ts W-501-b3 “a stale token on a new mount after an earlier success re-reads once”
2. advisory — brief:139 “A dropped live stream” overpromises: b3 expressly makes an ordinarily reconnecting stream issue no check read and owe no remount; only an authentication-refused, closed stream does. Replace brief:139 with: `5. Once a screen has loaded, saving a new token just closes the prompt, so a half-written answer is kept; you then press the button again. The screen reloads its data only when it never got its data—a fresh tab or stale token before the current screen loaded—or when the live stream is authentication-refused and closed; an ordinarily dropped, reconnecting stream does not reload it. Agree?` [severity: S2] [class: spec×prose-contradiction-under-revision] — check: apps/web/test/w501.test.ts W-501-b3 “a reconnecting stream issues no read”
